WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.042
Hi! Butterflies, leaves and many letters are symmetric. Today we'll learn about symmetric figures, find lines of symmetry, and complete half a figure.

2
00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:24.234
If a figure can be folded along a straight line so that the two halves match exactly, it is symmetric. That line is called a line of symmetry. It can go up and down, across, or on a slant.

3
00:00:24.384 --> 00:00:30.426
The letters A, H, M and T have a line of symmetry. F and G do not.

4
00:00:30.576 --> 00:00:42.258
To check if a line is a line of symmetry, imagine folding along it. If you fold a rectangle along its diagonal, the halves don't match, so the diagonal is not a line of symmetry.

5
00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:49.194
But a square folded along its diagonal matches exactly, so for a square it is.

6
00:00:49.344 --> 00:00:57.138
Let's complete a symmetric figure on a grid. The red dashed line is the line of symmetry, and the left half is drawn.

7
00:00:57.288 --> 00:01:06.258
Take each corner point. Count how many squares it is from the line, then mark a point the same number of squares on the other side, in the same row.

8
00:01:06.408 --> 00:01:14.898
Finally, join the points in order and the figure is complete. Fold it, and both halves match exactly.

9
00:01:15.048 --> 00:01:22.170
Watch out! Many pupils think a rectangle's diagonal is a line of symmetry. It's not!

10
00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:28.770
Fold a paper rectangle along its diagonal and the corners stick out. They don't match.

11
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:37.938
A rectangle has just two lines of symmetry: one across and one down, each through the middles of opposite sides.

12
00:01:38.088 --> 00:01:47.154
Your turn! Which of the letters F, T and G is symmetric? Pause and think.

13
00:01:47.304 --> 00:01:55.266
It's T. Fold it along the middle line going down, and both halves match. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:55.416 --> 00:02:04.434
Another one! How many lines of symmetry does a square have? Pause and think.

15
00:02:04.584 --> 00:02:12.042
It has 4: one across, one down and the two diagonals. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:12.192 --> 00:02:21.306
Next one! How many lines of symmetry does the letter H have? Pause and think.

17
00:02:21.456 --> 00:02:33.090
It has 2: one going down through the middle, and one going across through the middle bar. Fold along either line and the halves match exactly. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:44.850
Last one! A point is 3 squares to the left of the line of symmetry. Where is its matching point? Pause and think.

19
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.498
It's 3 squares to the right of the line, in the same row. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:51.648 --> 00:03:04.314
Remember: it's a line of symmetry only if both halves match exactly when folded. Imagine folding to check. To complete a figure, put each point in the same row, the same distance from the line.

21
00:03:04.464 --> 00:03:09.930
Fold a piece of paper and cut out your own symmetric shape!

